WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:15.751
Unit six: Local Places & Landmarks. In this unit, you will describe famous places in your town or city.

4
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.681
Landmark.

5
00:00:18.381 --> 00:00:21.635
Landmark means a famous place that is easy to recognize.

6
00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:24.190
The Independence Monument is a landmark.

7
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.809
Your turn. Say: Landmark.

8
00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:31.475
Landmark.

9
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:33.461
Monument.

10
00:00:34.161 --> 00:00:38.100
Monument means a building or statue made to remember someone or something.

11
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.167
There is a monument in the park.

12
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:43.159
Your turn. Say: Monument.

13
00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:46.710
Monument.

14
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:48.567
Museum.

15
00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:52.799
Museum means a building where you can see old or important things.

16
00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:55.656
The National Museum has ancient statues.

17
00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.275
Your turn. Say: Museum.

18
00:01:01.975 --> 00:01:03.046
Museum.

19
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.016
Historic.

20
00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:07.913
Historic means important in history.

21
00:01:08.213 --> 00:01:10.515
Phnom Penh has many historic buildings.

22
00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:13.809
Your turn. Say: Historic.

23
00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.603
Historic.

24
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:19.351
Visit.

25
00:01:20.051 --> 00:01:22.619
Visit means to go to see a place or a person.

26
00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:24.988
Many people visit the Royal Palace.

27
00:01:25.688 --> 00:01:28.027
Your turn. Say: Visit.

28
00:01:30.727 --> 00:01:31.554
Visit.

29
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.319
Local.

30
00:01:34.019 --> 00:01:36.529
Local means from or in the area where you live.

31
00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.701
We buy fruit at the local market.

32
00:01:39.401 --> 00:01:41.984
Your turn. Say: Local.

33
00:01:44.684 --> 00:01:45.453
Local.

34
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.567
Famous.

35
00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.371
Famous means known by many people.

36
00:01:50.671 --> 00:01:53.124
Angkor Wat is famous all over the world.

37
00:01:53.824 --> 00:01:56.128
Your turn. Say: Famous.

38
00:01:58.828 --> 00:01:59.689
Famous.

39
00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:01.394
Tourist.

40
00:02:02.094 --> 00:02:05.313
Tourist means a person who travels to visit a place for fun.

41
00:02:05.613 --> 00:02:07.496
Tourists take photos at Wat Phnom.

42
00:02:08.196 --> 00:02:10.628
Your turn. Say: Tourist.

43
00:02:13.328 --> 00:02:14.236
Tourist.

44
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.261
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:17.561 --> 00:02:20.060
Sreypich, what landmarks are there in Phnom Penh?

46
00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.452
There is the Royal Palace, and there are many museums.

47
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.471
Is there a famous monument?

48
00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:31.027
Yes, there is the Independence Monument.

49
00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:33.898
Do many tourists visit it?

50
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:38.103
Yes! Tourists take photos there every day.

51
00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:42.264
Grammar focus: There is/are plus landmark.

52
00:02:42.564 --> 00:02:45.878
There is a famous palace. There are many museums.

53
00:02:46.178 --> 00:02:48.851
Use 'there is' for one thing and 'there are' for two or more.

54
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.560
Now read and listen. Landmarks in My City.

55
00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.452
I live in Phnom Penh, the capital of Cambodia.

56
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.017
There is a beautiful Royal Palace near the river.

57
00:03:00.317 --> 00:03:03.082
There are many historic buildings and local markets.

58
00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:07.416
There is also the National Museum with ancient statues.

59
00:03:08.717 --> 00:03:12.609
Every year, thousands of tourists visit these famous landmarks.

60
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:16.476
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:16.776 --> 00:03:18.752
blank many museums in the city.

62
00:03:19.052 --> 00:03:22.671
A, There are. B, There is. C, It is.

63
00:03:26.683 --> 00:03:28.927
The answer is A: There are.

64
00:03:30.417 --> 00:03:33.600
A person who travels to visit a place for fun is a blank.

65
00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.356
A, tourist. B, monument. C, landmark.

66
00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:43.315
The answer is A: tourist.

67
00:03:44.817 --> 00:03:46.607
Known by many people is blank.

68
00:03:46.907 --> 00:03:51.664
A, famous. B, local. C, historic.

69
00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.137
The answer is A: famous.

70
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.289
Now it's your turn to speak. What is a famous landmark in your town?

71
00:04:08.589 --> 00:04:13.923
There is a famous pagoda in my town. There are also old French buildings, and many tourists visit them.

72
00:04:14.223 --> 00:04:16.153
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:21.486
Great work today! You learned eight new words and there is/are plus landmark.

74
00:04:21.786 --> 00:04:26.365
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

75
00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:28.981
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

76
00:04:29.281 --> 00:04:31.899
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

